WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
<v Mike>Deja vu.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.680
<v Mike>In this case, what you don't know can kill you.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:29.300
<v Mike>And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.380
<v Hosts>I'm Mike.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.520
<v Hosts>Hey Mike. Oh, I'm Sean.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.260
<v Hosts>And I'm Joe.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.300
<v Mike>Ironically, maybe, deja vu is about amnesia.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.560
<v Joe>Yeah? I think that that's true.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.880
<v Mike>I accept this.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.460
<v Mike>Both as a video game and as a term.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.540
<v Sean>Yes. The word means kind.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.720
<v Joe>No, it actually doesn't.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:01.340
<v Mike>It doesn't, right? But experiencing deja vu is a form of amnesia.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.300
<v Mike>It's future amnesia. Yeah.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.300
<v Joe>I think we'd be like misrepresenting what deja vu is.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:19.380
<v Joe>But I think if you have amnesia and then you suddenly get like a memory starts coming back to you that you used to have, that would feel like deja vu.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.800
<v Joe>It's like, oh, I feel like this moment's happened before because you're remembering something that happened before.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.240
<v Joe>Whereas deja vu, I know, is actually just like something that you're living in right now.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.940
<v Joe>And it feels like you already have that memory.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.180
<v Joe>So they're like adjacent.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.480
<v Joe>So it's kind of like, you know, we're not we're not being literal with deja vu.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.160
<v Sean>But yeah, there's still like brain brain not do good work good sometimes.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.240
<v Mike>Exactly.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:48.440
<v Mike>And what deja vu is, is it's a point and click adventure game set in 1941 Chicago.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:02:04.100
<v Mike>You're a private investigator, Ace Harding, who suffers from amnesia, awakes in a bathroom stall and slowly unravels a case that actually involves him.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.860
<v Mike>This is just an NES port.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:18.360
<v Mike>It's not exclusive to the console, but it is kind of in line with some of the other point and click games that we've had on the show.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:25.360
