<v Sean>I think that all of the systems, like, the technical aspects, like, just the way everything's

01:32:37.860 --> 01:32:40.520
<v Sean>set up, it felt a lot more streamlined.

01:32:40.760 --> 01:32:44.600
<v Sean>I don't even know how stream, maybe it wasn't more streamlined than Shadowgate.

01:32:44.840 --> 01:32:50.740
<v Joe>But this felt more, like, holistically designed to me than Shadowgate.

01:32:50.860 --> 01:32:58.540
<v Sean>But unfortunately, this game really, really got on my nerves in some very specific ways,

01:32:58.540 --> 01:33:00.600
<v Sean>like I just described.

01:33:00.600 --> 01:33:09.380
<v Sean>I think that if there was some way to find change in the couch cushions somewhere, other

01:33:09.380 --> 01:33:10.460
<v Mike>than in the casino.

01:33:11.160 --> 01:33:21.360
<v Sean>And I was able to progress without having to reset in a way that's, like, not like, I don't

01:33:21.360 --> 01:33:26.000
<v Sean>know. I feel like there are reasons to say that, like, all right, this is, you failed, this is

01:33:26.000 --> 01:33:33.920
<v Sean>a lost state. But to have it so far into something that's not easy to roll back from, it's kind of a

01:33:33.920 --> 01:33:34.980
<v Sean>cardinal sin for me.

01:33:35.200 --> 01:33:40.020
<v Sean>Like, it's a typical, like, a typical adventure game sin.

01:33:40.740 --> 01:33:44.420
<v Sean>And I don't think that really existed in Shadowgate.

01:33:44.540 --> 01:33:50.360
<v Sean>And I think that Shadowgate also gets the benefit of novelty, where it was sort of the first

01:33:50.360 --> 01:33:52.060
<v Sean>time we had seen something like this.

01:33:53.360 --> 01:34:00.900
<v Sean>So I think this one might have more of a lasting impression on me, but it really peeved me.

01:34:00.900 --> 01:34:04.740
<v Sean>So I don't know if I could, if I can vote essential, even though it doesn't really matter at this

01:34:04.740 --> 01:34:06.040
<v Sean>point. All right.

01:34:06.520 --> 01:34:12.740
<v Mike>Uh, to close the loop on the Shadowgate talk, I would also just throw in that I feel like

01:34:12.740 --> 01:34:18.360
<v Mike>Shadowgate is more rewarding gameplay, like, moment to moment.

01:34:18.520 --> 01:34:24.380
<v Mike>Like, you're solving what we're calling puzzles quickly and all the time.

01:34:24.660 --> 01:34:30.500
<v Mike>Whereas, like, you can get kind of stuck in deja vu and just wander about, and that doesn't

01:34:30.500 --> 01:34:31.740
<v Mike>feel as good.

01:34:31.960 --> 01:34:33.020
<v Mike>So there's more of like a...

01:34:33.020 --> 01:34:40.540
<v Sean>But I do prefer, I do prefer the idea of solving a murder mystery than, like, escaping a bunch

01:34:40.540 --> 01:34:45.420
